-- Project configuration
--
-- TWO IMPLEMENTATIONS, TWO BUILDS, and the domain already has the shape for it:
-- `Project.language` / `Project.build` are `Option[T = String]` — ONE each — because
-- the multi-language carrier is `Module`, whose `language` is required and whose
-- `build` is its own. So the project-level pair names the PRIMARY (rustland is the
-- reference implementation) and the modules state the rest.
--
-- `tools` is the conservative project-wide default acceptance set. When
-- `anthill-todo add` / `insert` receives no explicit `--acceptance`, it embeds every
-- name below in the new WorkItem: this avoids guessing module ownership from prose
-- and ensures a cross-language ticket cannot silently omit the gate that observes
-- its change. Callers can still pass one or more `--acceptance` flags to narrow or
-- replace the default deliberately.

fact Project(
  name: "anthill",
  language: "rust",
  build: "cargo",
  modules: ["rustland", "scaland"],
  tools: ["cargo-test", "scaland-sbt-test"])

fact Module(name: "rustland", root: "rustland", language: "rust", build: "cargo")
fact Module(name: "scaland", root: "scaland", language: "scala", build: "sbt")

-- WHICH STORE HOLDS THESE WORK ITEMS, AND IN WHICH ROLE (proposal 057
-- §"Configuration & bootstrap"; WI-830). The host reads this at startup, maps the
-- declared store to one of its compiled-in backends, and registers it.
--
-- `mirror`, not `owner`, because the extent is RESIDENT: every file here is parsed
-- at startup and `kb.rules` answers every read, with the store as the write-through
-- durability leg. An `owner` would mean delegating reads to a query engine over
-- parsed text, for data already wholly in memory.
--
-- `root: "."` is this directory — the one the config lives in. The host resolves it;
-- a config file has no business naming an absolute path.
--
-- `covers` is the set of functors this file durably holds, and it is the set the
-- bundle persists. A functor missing here keeps no durable home: its retract would
-- drop the in-memory row and leave the line on disk.
--
-- NO `MirrorEntry`, AND THAT IS NOT AN OMISSION (WI-1117). The link row exists only
-- for a project that publishes to a mirror, and this one declares no `Mirror` fact,
-- so it can hold none — which is why the coverage check asks for it only of a
-- project that HAS a mirror. Naming it here anyway would be decoration, and
-- decoration is not free: `covers` is resolved at startup, so an entry naming a
-- functor a given BINARY does not define is a hard refusal, and every checkout
-- whose `anthill-todo` predates that functor stops working the moment it pulls.
-- That is §14.1's "backend before declaration, always", and the declaration is due
-- the day this repo configures a mirror — not before.
fact anthill.persistence.ExtentBinding(
  store: anthill.persistence.filesystem.ItemPerFileStore(
    root: ".",
    status_field: "last_status_change.status",
    id_field: "id",
    ref_field: "workitem"),
  role: anthill.persistence.ExtentRole.mirror(),
  covers: [WorkItem, Feedback, Tag, StoreFormat])
